  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cities with rights</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project proposes a national articulation for the Right to the City, based on urban collectives, UNITAS partners and allies, to promote inclusive, sustainable and resilient cities.
The aim is to achieve the strengthening of strategic competencies and capacity building in urban collectives and organisations of people in vulnerable situations, promoting spaces for multi-stakeholder dialogue to influence and contribute to the solution of urban problems at the local level and the implementation of urban initiatives aimed at promoting urban policy proposals for the transformation of cities, based on the implementation of the Urban Innovation Laboratory whose experiences will be collected in a technological package of know-how in cities.</narrative>
  </description>
